# The devcontainer build context is the repository root, but the image copies only the three
# files re-included below (see .devcontainer/Dockerfile). Everything else stays out of the
# context, so a growing project never slows a rebuild or leaks a file into the image.
# A project Dockerfile built from the root needs its own rules: BuildKit reads a
# <Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore for that Dockerfile before falling back to this file.
*
!.ai/RULES.md
!.devcontainer/managed-settings.json
!.devcontainer/project.sh
